## Blocks

```mdl
api A-1: the wasm back end
  signatures: Wasm.compile : (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> Text -> Text -> {Throw Text | e} List Int
```

```mdl
law L-1: a comparison on Int or Bool compiles as before, with no added function
  theorem: WasmEquality.Spec.scalarAddsNothing
  evidence: proof
```

```mdl
req R-1: == on a constructed value whose type is known compiles
  by: WasmEquality.Spec.optionEquality | WasmEquality.Spec.constructorAgainstNullary | WasmEquality.Spec.userTypeParameter
```

```mdl
req R-2: != on a constructed value compiles as the negation of ==
  by: WasmEquality.Spec.optionInequality
```

```mdl
req R-3: each instantiated type gets one function, shared by every comparison and by its own recursion
  by: WasmEquality.Spec.oneFunctionPerType | WasmEquality.Spec.nestedTypeTwoFunctions | WasmEquality.Spec.recursiveTypeOneFunction
```

```mdl
req R-4: order on data, a type with a type variable left in it, and a function field stay refused
  by: WasmEquality.Spec.orderRefused | WasmEquality.Spec.variableRefused | WasmEquality.Spec.functionFieldRefused
```
